<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 28,632,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 28,632,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 10/17/96    10/16/96	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 28,632,000  27,888,000    28,021,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	33,990,000  33,990,000    33,842,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,637,015  34,637,015	     N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 239,869	92,066	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   10/23/96    10/16/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,120,000   5,069,000     5,130,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,678,000   4,474,000     4,466,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,564,000   4,057,000     4,774,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,193,000   3,069,000     2,790,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,880,000   4,095,000     3,643,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,225,000   5,143,000     5,180,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,972,000   1,982,000     2,038,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	28,632,000  27,888,000    28,021,000</p>
